    "notes": "1. 'Total revenues and other income' is mapped to 'total_revenue' and is the sum of its three listed components. 2. 'Total costs and other deductions' is not used directly. Instead, 'total_operating_cost' is constructed from all cost line items above 'Income (loss) before income taxes', excluding 'Interest expense' and 'Other taxes and duties'. This follows standard practice for an integrated oil & gas company where operating costs include cost of sales (crude/product purchases), production, SG&A, depreciation/depletion, exploration, and pension expense. 3. 'Other taxes and duties' (e.g., property, severance, excise taxes) are considered part of the cost of revenue and are therefore included in 'total_operating_cost' via the 'Production and manufacturing expenses' and 'Selling, general and administrative expenses' lines, as detailed in Note 19. They are not listed separately in the output to avoid double-counting. 4. 'Net income' is mapped to the line attributable to the parent company. 5. 'Interest expense' is mapped directly. 6. All numbers are positive as per the statement; the sign convention rule (13) is applied conceptually: these are all expenses that reduce income, so they are reported as positive values in the output array. 7. Supplementary tables provide detail but do not alter the primary income statement line items used for extraction.",
